\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Christ Jesus lay in death's strong
\par For our offences given;   [bands
\par But now at God's right hand He stands,
\par And brings us life from heaven:
\par Wherefore let us joyful be,
\par And sing to God right thankfully
\par Loud songs of Hallelujah! 
\par Hallelujah!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. It was a strange and dreadful strife,
\par When life and death contended;
\par The victory remained with Life,
\par The reign of death was ended:
\par Stript of power, no more he reigns
\par An empty form alone remains;
\par His sting is lost for ever.
\par Hallelujah!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. So let us keep the festival
\par Where to Lord invites us;
\par Christ to Himself the joy of all,
\par The Sun that warms and lights us;
\par By His grace He doth impart
\par Eternal sunshine to the heart;
\par The night of sin is ended.
\par Hallelujah!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Then let us feast this Easter day
\par On the true Bread of heaven.
\par The word of grace hath purged away
\par The old and wicked leaven:
\par Christ alone our soul will feed,
\par He is pour meat and drink indeed,
\par Faith lives upon no other.
\par Hallelujah! 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

